tions 2027?]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bjps-third-term-bid-congresss-comeback-hopes-what-will-decide-uttarakhand-elections-2027/articleshow/135679227.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135679227.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bjps-third-term-bid-congresss-comeback-hopes-what-will-decide-uttarakhand-elections-2027/articleshow/135679227.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bjps-third-term-bid-congresss-comeback-hopes-what-will-decide-uttarakhand-elections-2027/articleshow/135679227.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T17:02:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135680594,imgsize-180138.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Manipur census on hold till April 2027 as high court seeks answers from the Centre]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/manipur-census-on-hold-till-april-2027-as-high-court-seeks-answers-from-the-centre/articleshow/135679686.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135679686.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Manipur high court has ordered the postponement of the Census 2027 until late April 2027. This ruling aims to address significant concerns regarding how recent ethnic violence and subsequent displacements might skew population counts. The court requested the Census Commissioner to review seven representations. Following the authorities' decision, a further four-week delay will apply, allowing anyone unhappy with the outcome to seek legal recourse.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/manipur-census-on-hold-till-april-2027-as-high-court-seeks-answers-from-the-centre/articleshow/135679686.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/manipur-census-on-hold-till-april-2027-as-high-court-seeks-answers-from-the-centre/articleshow/135679686.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T16:45:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135679863,imgsize-185304.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Karnataka, Keralam governments launch E20 petrol quality checks amid ethanol blending concerns]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/karnataka-keralam-governments-launch-e20-petrol-quality-checks-amid-ethanol-blending-concerns/articleshow/135676145.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135676145.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Keralam civil supplies department conducted inspections of petrol pumps in Kochi to examine the ethanol mix in E20 petrol. Officials took six samples, forwarding two for lab tests in Kakinada. Rising concerns over high ethanol blending have been highlighted by Karnataka Minister Rizwan Arshad. However, the union ministry of petroleum claims all samples adhere to quality norms, disputing allegations of excessive mixing.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/karnataka-keralam-governments-launch-e20-petrol-quality-checks-amid-ethanol-blending-concerns/articleshow/135676145.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/karnataka-keralam-governments-launch-e20-petrol-quality-checks-amid-ethanol-blending-concerns/articleshow/135676145.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T16:31:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135679782,imgsize-86650.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[India, Lebanon hold first Foreign Office consultations; discuss trade, investment, digital cooperation]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-lebanon-hold-first-foreign-office-consultations-discuss-trade-investment-digital-cooperation/articleshow/135677902.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135677902.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[India and Lebanon embarked on their first-ever Foreign Office Consultations in New Delhi, aiming to strengthen their bilateral relationship. Important topics of discussion included cooperation in political-security, economic, and socio-cultural arenas. Ambassador Sripriya Ranganathan's visit to Lebanon set the stage for deeper ties, as key areas like trade, investment, digital infrastructure, and pharmaceuticals were reviewed, along with pressing regional and international matters.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-lebanon-hold-first-foreign-office-consultations-discuss-trade-investment-digital-cooperation/articleshow/135677902.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-lebanon-hold-first-foreign-office-consultations-discuss-trade-investment-digital-cooperation/articleshow/135677902.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T16:01:43+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135679288,imgsize-64392.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['He called us Naxals': Rahul Gandhi hits back at PM Modi, renews debate challenge]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/he-called-us-naxals-rahul-gandhi-hits-back-at-pm-modi-renews-debate-challenge/articleshow/135678276.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135678276.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/he-called-us-naxals-rahul-gandhi-hits-back-at-pm-modi-renews-debate-challenge/articleshow/135678276.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/he-called-us-naxals-rahul-gandhi-hits-back-at-pm-modi-renews-debate-challenge/articleshow/135678276.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T15:41:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vivek Dubey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135678394,imgsize-1081662.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Semantically ignorant': Congress defends Kharge's 'Diwali a khushiyon ki Eid' remark]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/semantically-ignorant-congress-defends-kharges-diwali-a-khushiyon-ki-eid-remark/articleshow/135677989.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135677989.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Congress chief Mallikarjun Kharge stirred controversy by referring to Diwali as 'khushiyon ka Eid'. BJP officials accused the Congress of misrepresenting Diwali, asserting each festival has its unique identity. Pawan Khera of Congress defended Kharge's statement, emphasizing the meaning of 'Eid' as 'festival.' The BJP responded by questioning the appropriateness of comparing Diwali with Eid, which they deemed disrespectful. This disagreement highlights ongoing political tensions regarding religious and cultural identities.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/semantically-ignorant-congress-defends-kharges-diwali-a-khushiyon-ki-eid-remark/articleshow/135677989.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/semantically-ignorant-congress-defends-kharges-diwali-a-khushiyon-ki-eid-remark/articleshow/135677989.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T15:33:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135678202,imgsize-79979.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Delhi pollution sparks row: BJP alleges 'conspiracy'; AAP and Congress question AQI data]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhi-pollution-sparks-row-bjp-alleges-conspiracy-aap-and-congress-question-aqi-data/articleshow/135674399.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135674399.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhi-pollution-sparks-row-bjp-alleges-conspiracy-aap-and-congress-question-aqi-data/articleshow/135674399.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhi-pollution-sparks-row-bjp-alleges-conspiracy-aap-and-congress-question-aqi-data/articleshow/135674399.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T13:09:51+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vivek Dubey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135675068,imgsize-57608.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Jaishankar extends national day greetings to Cambodia, hails strong civilisational ties]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jaishankar-extends-national-day-greetings-to-cambodia-hails-strong-civilisational-ties/articleshow/135674222.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135674222.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[S Jaishankar conveyed warm National Day wishes to Cambodia, celebrating the deep-rooted civilizational connections between the two countries. He praised the successful conclusion of the recent Cambodia-India Bilateral Army Exercise, CINBAX-II, which focused on collaborative training to bolster operational synergy among their armed forces. The exercise allowed both teams to display their professionalism and exchange valuable operational insights, further solidifying the defense partnership between India and Cambodia.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jaishankar-extends-national-day-greetings-to-cambodia-hails-strong-civilisational-ties/articleshow/135674222.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jaishankar-extends-national-day-greetings-to-cambodia-hails-strong-civilisational-ties/articleshow/135674222.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T12:35:39+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135674342,imgsize-55916.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['True colours exposed': BJP's Giriraj Singh tears into Kharge over Diwali 'khushiyon ka Eid' remark]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/true-colours-exposed-bjps-giriraj-singh-tears-into-kharge-over-diwali-khushiyon-ka-eid-remark/articleshow/135673230.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135673230.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/true-colours-exposed-bjps-giriraj-singh-tears-into-kharge-over-diwali-khushiyon-ka-eid-remark/articleshow/135673230.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/true-colours-exposed-bjps-giriraj-singh-tears-into-kharge-over-diwali-khushiyon-ka-eid-remark/articleshow/135673230.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T11:50:08+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vivek Dubey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135673388,imgsize-1327014.cms"/></item></channel></rss>